cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AISME — AI Sessions Manager & Security Engine"
message: "If you use this work or its design documents, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alcober
    given-names: Eduardo
repository-code: "https://github.com/ealcober/AI-SYSTEM-MONITOR"
abstract: >-
  Kernel-level observability and containment for autonomous AI coding agents.
  AISME correlates what an AI agent declares it will do with what it actually
  does to the machine, and enforces the difference at the operating-system
  boundary. It includes a tiered enforcement design that provides in-kernel
  denial without a reboot, a permission model derived from Android's runtime
  permissions with a suppression discipline that never removes evidence, and a
  detection catalogue of deterministic joins over a causal provenance graph.
keywords:
  - AI agent security
  - eBPF
  - runtime security
  - prompt injection
  - provenance
  - Landlock
  - policy language
license: Apache-2.0
